      "headline": "Daniel Grayling Fogelberg (August 13, 1951 – December…",
      "supportingCopy": "Daniel Grayling Fogelberg (August 13, 1951 – December 16, 2007) was an American singer, songwriter, and multi-instrumentalist widely known for his 1970s and 1980s soft rock hits, including \"Longer\" (1979), \"Same Old Lang Syne\" (1980), and \"Leader of the Band\" (1981). He was the youngest of three sons born to Margaret (née Irvine, 1920–2015), a classically trained pianist, and Lawrence Peter Fogelberg (1911–1982), a band director at Woodruff High School in Peoria, at Pekin Community High School in Pekin, Illinois, and at Bradley University in Peoria.",
